17.3 Release 4.1.0 [2025-06-25]
===============================

   * New features:

        + Publish binary wheel packages on PyPI(1) with support for
          multiple operating systems (Linux, macOS, Windows), processor
          architectures (AMD64, ARM64), MPI implementations (MPICH, Open
          MPI, and their ABI-compatible derivatives), and Python
          implementations (CPython, PyPy).

        + Add support for the MPI 5.0 standard.

             - MPI handle serialization with integral values.

             - Fixed-size Fortran ‘LOGICAL’ datatypes.

             - Query ABI version/info and Fortran ABI info.

        + *note MPI.Datatype.Create_contiguous: 340. now uses
          BigMPI(2)’s approach when using MPI implementations that do
          not yet support the MPI 4.0 large-count APIs.

        + Add support for *note MPI.FLOAT16_T: 588. and *note
          MPI.BFLOAT16_T: 58b. datatypes.  These datatypes are not yet
          standard but available as extensions in MPI implementations.

        + Add *note MPI.Status.tomemory: 4ae. to expose the status
          contents as a memoryview(3) object.

   * Enhancements:

        + Support (opt-in via *note MPI4PY_BUILD_PYSABI: 807.) for
          building with Py_LIMITED_API(4) under Python 3.10+ (requires
          Cython 3.1+).

        + Support (opt-in via *note MPI4PY_BUILD_MPIABI: 806.) for
          building with the MPI 5.0 standard ABI and the MPICH or Open
          MPI legacy ABIs.  The *note MPI: 3. extension module will be
          able to dynamically link at runtime with older versions (down
          to the MPI 3.0 standard) of the MPI implementation used at
          compile time.  Only available on Linux, macOS, and Windows.

        + Support a ‘buffersize’ parameter in the *note
          MPIPoolExecutor.map(): 223. and *note
          MPIPoolExecutor.starmap(): 224. methods to limit the number of
          pending tasks.

        + Improve ownership management of DLPack capsules.

        + Reimplement MPI DLL search path on Windows.

        + Minor fixes to typing stubs and documentation.

   * Backward-incompatible changes:

        + Python 3.8+ is required.

        + The *note MPI.Exception: 9e. class is now a heap type.

        + The types of the *note MPI.BOTTOM: fa, *note MPI.IN_PLACE: fc,
          and *note MPI.BUFFER_AUTOMATIC: fe. are no longer subclasses
          of int(5).

   ---------- Footnotes ----------

   (1) https://pypi.org/project/mpi4py/#files

   (2) https://doi.org/10.1109/ExaMPI.2014.5

   (3) https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#memoryview

   (4) https://docs.python.org/3/c-api/stable.html#c.Py_LIMITED_API

   (5) https://docs.python.org/3/library/functions.html#int


